# pulsemon release-signing public keys (ed25519, hex, one per line).
#
# A release binary is accepted only if its detached .sig asset verifies
# against at least one key below. This is the authenticity root for
# self-update: a compromised release pipeline can publish a binary and its
# SHA-256 (both come from the same release), but it cannot sign the binary
# without the private key, so the client refuses to install it.
#
# Rotation: add the new pubkey on its own line, ship a release signed by the
# new key, then retire the old key in a LATER release (keep both until the
# fleet is off the old key). The set — not a single key — is what makes
# rotation a normal update instead of a full re-bootstrap.
#
# Generated 2026-10-29. The matching private key is the release-signing
# secret: it lives on the trusted release host and (for the Windows CI path)
# as the RELEASE_SIGNING_KEY secret. It is NEVER committed.
